src/vendor/mcode-background-task/ contains eight files from
packages/agent-modules/background-task/src. Relative import suffixes change
from .js to .ts. The error constructor uses an explicit field instead of a
parameter property. These changes support native Node type stripping.

src/vendor/mcode-child-bash/ contains child-bash-lifecycle.ts and
task-waiter-registry.ts from packages/local-runtime/src/background-task.
The lifecycle imports use child-bash-ports.ts instead of MCode host services.
The lifecycle and waiter bodies are unchanged. The sync script verifies
and reverses each import change. Pi adapters use this lifecycle for owned
native commands and result delivery within the same logical task.

src/file-write-targets.ts reuses the pure target-extraction helpers from
packages/local-runtime/src/turns/file-changes.ts. Pi supplies its brand path
and metadata observation port, without the MCode diff or database host.
Two narrow path ports preserve literal whitespace and treat unresolved
shell parent traversal as ambiguous before lexical path resolution.
test/fixtures/file-observation/upstream-file-changes.ts.txt preserves the
original source. Offline tests check its hash and the helper bodies with
these explicit ports.

src/task-turn-id.ts preserves the upstream task-turn ID encoding.
Task admission, continuation, terminal output and tool-result adapters also
follow the upstream task protocol. The unchanged MIT reference sources in
test/fixtures/mcode-task-steering/ and mcode-task-terminal/ support offline
task-protocol tests. They are not a bundled host runtime.

upstream.lock.json records vendor and task-reference hashes. The role prompts
are maintained for this plugin. src/task-verification.ts adapts the upstream
verdict parser; test/fixtures/task-verification/upstream.ts.txt preserves the
reference used by its differential tests. The unchanged local-task-control.ts
reference in test/fixtures/task-lineage/ checks public continuation lineage.
Core role, model and child-surface references are monitored for manual review;
they are not copied into the Pi runtime. Programmatic tool calls map upstream
PTC to native Pi codemode, not to a separate PTC host. Workspace observations use bounded
Pi-side metadata snapshots, not the MCode observation database. Child sessions, tools and resources use the
host Pi SDK. This package does not reproduce the MCode host platform.

sdk-patches/ contains a source patch for @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent 1.5.0
at earendil-works/pi revision f9a26365568127461c47a07a37dcb42c140a3ac5.
The patch adds an accepted-resource snapshot interface. It does not install
or replace the host SDK. The original SDK uses the MIT license, included in
sdk-patches/LICENSE-PI. Its seven base files match the pinned upstream source.
